text I look on as Nagisa performs.
text Her homemade script is clutched in her hands.
text The play goes exactly as she explained it to me.
text A girl who's been left all alone in the world creates a doll out of junk she collects.
text When she does, it comes to life, and the girl stops being sad.
text All's well that ends well.
text Honestly, the story might be perfect for the short amount of time she's been given.
text Watching Nagisa practice, I suddenly remember what seemed to be a feeling of deja vu I had when I first heard about the story.
text I was hoping that something somewhere deep in my memories would come back to me by seeing Nagisa's performance, but nothing has.
text The play isn't complete enough.
text @[Tomoya]
text (No... I doubt this story will ever be completed.)
text That's the feeling I'm getting.
text There are just too few clues.
text And I'm the only one looking for the answer, anyway.
text Nagisa already seems satisfied with what she has.
text If I worry about anything, it should be about taking care of her.
text And once Founder's Festival ends without incident...
text We can start acting more like a proper couple.
text For now though, my role is just to sit here and watch her.
